  "title": "Stationary marginals and bottleneck restrictions for Boolean Doob kernels",
  "abstract": "We study positive multiplicative transforms of the Boolean noise kernel with exact low-order stationary marginals. A stationary Lp bound for p greater than 1+rho yields quantitative convergence of the smoothed potential, Perron normalization and weighting density in Hellinger distance. A bounded family constructed from products of block majorities shows that uniform convergence of the potential can nevertheless fail. At the critical moment exponent and square-root marginal scale, an explicit comparison with an auxiliary weighting operator forces every sufficiently low-conductance cut to have exponentially small stationary mass. A separate bound excludes almost-unit killed modes on supports of exponentially small cardinality in a specified noise range, without marginal matching. The two exclusions leave an uncovered range and do not prove a dimension-uniform spectral gap for the actual stationary kernel. Complete proofs, imported programme dependencies and failed comparison routes are retained. Classical finite matrix scaling is not claimed as new. No physical or continuum spectral-gap conclusion is drawn.",
  "authors": [
